    <!-- Consent Screen -->
    <string name="cd_privacy">Privacy</string>
    <string name="consent_title">Your Privacy Matters</string>
    <string name="consent_subtitle">Before using BirdoVPN, please review how your data is handled.</string>
    <!-- The pre-use data declaration (Apple 5.4 / Play prominent disclosure).
         Wording is REMEDIATION-DECISIONS §1.5, audit 2026-09-29 (P0-1 / B-1 /
         D-1 / B-3). The previous text claimed "RAM-only volatile
         infrastructure" and that no connection timestamps or IP addresses
         were logged; the nodes are ordinary disk-backed cloud servers and the
         account system does keep a live session record while you are
         connected. Never reintroduce "RAM-only", "volatile", "diskless",
         "zero logs" or "non-reversible". -->
    <string name="consent_no_logs_title">No Activity Logs</string>
    <string name="consent_no_logs_desc">Our VPN servers don\'t record the sites you visit, your DNS queries or your traffic. While you\'re connected, our account system keeps a live record of your session (server, device, connect time). It is deleted when you disconnect and is left out of our nightly backups. We also count your data use per billing period.</string>
    <string name="consent_minimal_data_title">What Your Account Holds</string>
    <string name="consent_minimal_data_desc">Your email (or anonymous account number), plan, the devices you add, and your usage totals. Full list: birdo.app/privacy.</string>
    <!-- OPT-IN, off by default: the switch next to this text starts unticked,
         and BirdoApp starts Sentry only if the user ticks it here or in
         Settings. Wording: REMEDIATION-DECISIONS §1.3 / §1.5 (audit
         2026-09-29; second-pass #7, option A: FaultReporter's non-fatal
         connect / kill-switch / stealth / PQ / DNS fault events are disclosed,
         not dropped). Do not reintroduce "anonymous", "no personal data" or
         "only" — a report carries device model and OS version, which are
         personal data. -->
    <string name="consent_crash_reports_title">Crash Reports (optional)</string>
    <string name="consent_crash_reports_desc">Off by default. If you turn this on, the app sends crash and error reports to Sentry so we can fix bugs: crashes, and errors when an app feature such as connecting or the kill switch fails, with the app and OS version and device model. No account details, IP address or browsing data. Change it any time in Settings.</string>
